Sol's 4-slot g128 port (new internal GGML_TYPE_Q2_0_G128, gated by GGUF key
GGML_Q2_0_G128) applied to the branch: core type/traits + CPU kernels + gguf
loader gate/verify/remap (wired) + Vulkan registration. 7 context-drift rejects
applied surgically. BUILD FAILS at the Vulkan shader stage:
  copy_to_quant.comp:260 (set_rows_f16_q2_0_g128 permutation) —
  'data_s[src_idx+j] * id' multiplies float16_t (S_TYPE) by float; 11 glslc
  errors ('no operation * ... float16_t x float', 'float16 types can only be
  in uniform block or buffer storage: required extension not requested').
  Needs a float() cast on the half source, Sol's shader-correctness call.
NOT merged to master. Verify legs not run (no binary).

